{"step_index":99,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T14:15:08Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T18:15:08+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T18:15:12+04:00\nThe search for \"site:github.com/yctimlin/mcp_excalidraw \"mcpServers\"\" returned the following summary:\nThe GitHub repository `yctimlin/mcp_excalidraw` provides an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server and agent skill designed to allow AI agents to interact with Excalidraw, enabling them to programmatically create, edit, and export diagrams with real-time canvas synchronization[1][2].\n\n### Configuration for `mcpServers`\nTo use this MCP server with clients like Claude Desktop or Cursor, you need to add the appropriate configuration to your MCP configuration file (e.g., `claude_desktop_config.json` or `.cursor/mcp.json`)[3][4][5].\n\nWhile configuration can vary based on whether you are running it locally or via `npx`, here is the standard format often referenced for this repository[3][4][5]:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"mcp_excalidraw\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"excalidraw-mcp\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Notes on Configuration:**\n*   **Local Paths:** If you have cloned the repository and are running it from a local directory, you should point to the compiled `index.js` file[5][6]:\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"excalidraw\": {\n          \"command\": \"node\",\n          \"args\": [\"/absolute/path/to/mcp_excalidraw/dist/index.js\"]\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    ```\n*   **Environment Variables:** Depending on your setup, you may need to specify environment variables like `EXPRESS_SERVER_URL` to point to the canvas server[4][5].\n\nFor the most accurate instructions, please check the **README.md** file directly in the [yctimlin/mcp_excalidraw GitHub repository](https://github.com/yctimlin/mcp_excalidraw)[7], as command arguments or server names can sometimes change.\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE300B5vJUnCYrdNeM4OY_i5utgx5taJX9yNwI81OTZDRUVPnkpcbvjBlFbph3HwGUbuq1JqbX-ZEWHXm38vS7KXCDjbdn_mZs5TW4UPOfsweoT0sGDtxtLBoTjL4xiwhc=)\n[2] [mcp.so](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGKFWeUO8C3unlSdVEVoRTQaykGRMzIZgA_xtRt9_YJTW6PY6pmmmbN-9NPaZKk1mfee4Wu9PouPZsXhObc1JZ4wgGcqdDhJbEzVVkLUov8AopMLBoSE65qL55i)\n[3] [lobehub.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGS9_xmklgEaGynuGSEjWdEfEe8SkB_oyBcRms4biL24XxtG_rjY4z46ndgC4bg7FqK2h8x8l3ZxDMgd_8xYFn9cg-1GkgsvxEJSyhHdgvSU8bHxpXxL8mY_Nia9LsEpWx3bOxR4w==)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE300B5vJUnCYrdNeM4OY_i5utgx5taJX9yNwI81OTZDRUVPnkpcbvjBlFbph3HwGUbuq1JqbX-ZEWHXm38vS7KXCDjbdn_mZs5TW4UPOfsweoT0sGDtxtLBoTjL4xiwhc=)\n[5] [npmjs.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGQuWQzWxDSyUVQGh4TTd_aqS_O7JeLAI24_yAIcXWdWlvXjvnFXP8C99CZGtLGPJMoHDDjBEPBrxdTnYvfUyokKFbWe8gIZWDLkgYoikRbNO8uSANnpbatKOvoccvWtQ3dKFLEfXlTZ2Xi5RqYuOJiwGJb2cPm)\n[6] [lobehub.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH8K77zDmz7id2PjSUwLE2pyzR1Yc5RdEiDPumqvf8cLJ6lFKIZKeni9Rt_pL6d-8-5BHAsXf7INdj06t2Wc86xlnMxKi_vmMLM510-IZq6DA6l_ilYPVw8wAfLjPa6zaJUPJ8cNJGgiZZnrg==)\n[7] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE300B5vJUnCYrdNeM4OY_i5utgx5taJX9yNwI81OTZDRUVPnkpcbvjBlFbph3HwGUbuq1JqbX-ZEWHXm38vS7KXCDjbdn_mZs5TW4UPOfsweoT0sGDtxtLBoTjL4xiwhc=)"}
{"step_index":100,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T14:15:12Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"mcp-excalidraw-server\" \"Claude Desktop\"","toolAction":"Searching Claude Desktop config","toolSummary":"Search Claude Desktop config for mcp-excalidraw-server"}}]}
{"step_index":101,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T14:15:16Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T18:15:16+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T18:15:20+04:00\nThe search for \"\"mcp-excalidraw-server\" \"Claude Desktop\"\" returned the following summary:\n`mcp-excalidraw-server` is an **MCP (Model Context Protocol) server** designed to integrate Excalidraw's diagramming capabilities directly into AI agents, such as those running in **Claude Desktop**, Cursor, or other MCP-compatible clients[1][2][3].\n\n### What it does\nUnlike basic integrations that might only generate a static image, `mcp-excalidraw-server` provides a **persistent, interactive workbench** for AI agents[4][5][6]. It allows Claude to[1][6]:\n*   **Create and Modify:** Programmatically create, edit, update, or delete elements on an Excalidraw canvas[3][5].\n*   **Persistent Workflow:** Maintains the canvas state, allowing for iterative refinement of diagrams rather than one-off generations[7][6].\n*   **Advanced Control:** Offers tools for layout management, element-level control, screenshotting (so the AI can \"see\" what it has drawn), and file export[1][3][5].\n\n### How to use it with Claude Desktop\nTo use it with Claude Desktop, you typically configure the server in your `claude_desktop_config.json` file[8][9].\n\n1.  **Configuration:** You add the server to your configuration file, pointing to the local installation of the MCP server[8][9]. A typical configuration entry looks like this:\n    ```json\n    \"mcpServers\": {\n      \"excalidraw\": {\n        \"command\": \"node\",\n        \"args\": [\"/absolute/path/to/your/excalidraw-mcp/dist/index.js\"]\n      }\n    }\n    ```\n2.  **Usage:** Once configured and Claude Desktop is restarted, Claude will have access to the Excalidraw tools[9][10]. You can then prompt Claude in natural language to \"create an architecture diagram,\" \"visualize this code,\" or \"draw a flowchart,\" and it will use the MCP tools to interact with the canvas[2][11][10].\n\n### Important Distinction\nThere are different versions of Excalidraw MCP servers available:\n*   **`mcp-excalidraw-server` (e.g., by yctimlin):** This is the version often cited for power users and coding agents, focusing on persistent, multi-tool, agentic workflows[1][7][6].\n*   **Official/Other versions:** There are other implementations (including an official Excalidraw+ MCP) that may offer different features, such as simpler \"one-shot\" diagram generation or integration with Excalidraw's cloud services[12][13][6].\n\nIf you are looking for a robust, local-first experience where an AI agent can \"work\" alongside you on a diagram, the community-maintained `mcp-excalidraw` packages are generally the recommended path[1][7].\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGU0wmYaoo465FS-4ML2CvIZMq3zRmpfIsK5OlbN4BVWcINGWGfl6sPQzZgYFNdExwOdSplDMF746jUf4MYGnYkx2aNMuENr65V1uo8UCE5Dk6-CspRt1SiFn_8mPzJk70=)\n[2] [npmjs.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFn3E2WA1cnSdfUSAWl00DpnLdCCiOhBy3mix2c7zdjFivUaSKSPwWPRVHebFP-VEdsoZKG5grsxPHTzP9HXzmJxIzqSyInSKf2SuTP2mO0UvKXobXatrW7SMEbCQOyJQOL6zp4py5A6Mc4VVW9I3OEOHTKtClD)\n[3] [mcpagentsmarket.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHcA_BhgbbN1_sXlSpHM-RBerUNacikHHxfW_ZQqsItaICW8wAQEkj8-C7cEg0QydmMehsvgKfUKyMRxhvrrwQ1dXxsB3sqJ7XopUkgvRwIJrKfX-WRGZnN4cEYA8jH6jLZ13qU)\n[4] [skywork.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFJ7pFw0ZRIZHQQfWazKcSetiM3ZHpkFBwLF5zBFjU8_Azej6Xs74rLIbizfbftG-arfSVHKYbgohNCHS_xX7_XuR4YG1g59TSr5gWF0NU8_VV7NG0kCDK0JswCaXshO-RtiDjh9r0UKDb2kGHqwdbgR43kdS7KMpyRHtDTdTKA8jFftGqI1sy6)\n[5] [mcpservers.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHmFshqp0fLUzxNR-NsiYO1TwKHbBPGNBWO9rmbHgrDhiWeInyXi3XfGhrhGVKqUY8jzHlfAChBgTVdeS6F9M5ncB5_70MbZX6fdeLz0QMq52dfIc0N7pvb2QEVOjNqMDZEV3Nf8Rgm7nIOOiQ