{"step_index":103,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T14:15:28Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T18:15:28+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T18:15:34+04:00\nThe search for \"\"mcp-excalidraw-server\" \"mcp\" command args\" returned the following summary:\nTo configure the `mcp-excalidraw-server` (often referenced in the context of the **yctimlin/mcp_excalidraw** implementation), you typically define it as an MCP server within your AI client's configuration file (e.g., `claude_desktop_config.json` or `.cursor/mcp.json`)[1].\n\n### **Typical Configuration**\nMost users integrate this server using `npx` to ensure it uses the latest version without needing a manual local build[1].\n\n#### **Claude Desktop / Cursor Configuration**\nAdd the following to your MCP configuration file:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"excalidraw\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"mcp-excalidraw-server\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### **Common Command Line Arguments & Options**\nIf you are running the server directly via the CLI or need to pass specific configurations, here is the standard breakdown:\n\n*   **`npx -y mcp-excalidraw-server`**: The primary command to execute the server[2][3].\n*   **Environment Variables**: These are often used to configure the server's behavior, particularly for canvas synchronization[4]:\n    *   `EXPRESS_SERVER_URL`: Sets the URL for the local canvas server (e.g., `http://localhost:3000`)[4][5].\n    *   `ENABLE_CANVAS_SYNC`: Set to `true` to enable real-time synchronization between the AI agent and the canvas[4][5].\n*   **Debug/Help Options**:\n    *   `-d`, `--debug`: Enables debug logging[6].\n    *   `-?`, `--help`: Shows the help message[6].\n    *   `--yes`: Often used with commands like `clear` to skip confirmation prompts[7].\n\n### **Important Notes**\n*   **Local vs. Remote**: There are multiple Excalidraw MCP implementations. The setup above is for the common local Node.js-based server[1]. If you are using the official remote version or Excalidraw+, you may need to point to a URL (e.g., `https://api.excalidraw.com/api/v1/mcp`) and provide an API key via headers[8][9][10].\n*   **Absolute Paths**: If you have cloned the repository locally and are running from the source instead of `npx`, your `args` should point to the absolute path of the compiled file, typically:\n    `\"args\": [\"/absolute/path/to/mcp_excalidraw/dist/index.js\"]`[1].\n\nSources:\n[1] [lobehub.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEGKFhyqeDeGNEWRaRhB8XPvAAqbMGiSIDwMZt6fhe0VFGY4GiCqwuHo7g1hqOHT01wDdEBYWur7mLRz4Qu84hIM4kCSUU8C7O30SZMBPJXq_iqExuQK_YsHh8Ai_jJOr1IUgRVpFG1LefEsw==)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEnk9s7TSC8sDIh1BjsgBgvWiKk7xa-rkfQJsdHZRFFShgLlrmChQen0Y9CuStx3YE71DB1dCq9KzKz6tzWTJy9eSNMA2hFbz_If5p8R6RZi9hM9KEQ0b46XRLzByfxK9Y=)\n[3] [wordpress.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGyS4wKlYOHDBoQcUQR6WGL3FS1Nps_xMOoF2UKIVNrzLQgswsQFcftsigAcE_4WFlMIkh7Yi3HZtCMqSumpTKxNbR3faqYnRCHVrwiVZRiC0dsEZyTjvNnEaxLTEdT2NB2B_IEuCp9M6E5fZ6B7ApKU8ybJFgBIVbpU41JiAyUNQPoiO8zScZhCouQzr9eCNO7n_rrkQ1v-jpaU-RhdVBo9ntY2g==)\n[4] [npmjs.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFgDh6SQGlRFrAfvZ7zRBE04PrW1WQv6abLwMF5EiObadsVGdJWOh_wcdoDmI6eTXE1Ym8qWlRj-xYoriorTnc7wbEmq-YYcXMwzKYoMlvwwuWcjSPUi-loNSMca73q6KpQXGbgBNwpgtR623xCAe4ma9G-pXpO)\n[5] [wordpress.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGyS4wKlYOHDBoQcUQR6WGL3FS1Nps_xMOoF2UKIVNrzLQgswsQFcftsigAcE_4WFlMIkh7Yi3HZtCMqSumpTKxNbR3faqYnRCHVrwiVZRiC0dsEZyTjvNnEaxLTEdT2NB2B_IEuCp9M6E5fZ6B7ApKU8ybJFgBIVbpU41JiAyUNQPoiO8zScZhCouQzr9eCNO7n_rrkQ1v-jpaU-RhdVBo9ntY2g==)\n[6] [lobehub.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFfO7TfJQ_sA8X87Xj8SQQxa8E1bihODc1H0Ggu3JZ-ebZMVZh0h-9lTBkWnUh48N37I1X4lzQOGBLuLiCJSk14FmK45oQnHS3QEd9m